<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Library of Alexandria</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Library of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandria">Alexandria</a> was the great library founded under the Ptolemaic kings in Alexandria in the third century BCE, part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mouseion">Mouseion</a> research institution. It aimed to collect all known Greek writing and became the leading centre of scholarship in the Hellenistic world. It is one of the most celebrated legacies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ptolemaic-kingdom">Ptolemaic Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/library-of-alexandria.jpg" alt="Library of Alexandria" width="320" height="325" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: O. Von Corven · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ancientlibraryalex.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
